---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Review-screen anatomy">
  <p class="demo-note">
    Three patterns show a record for review — <a href={base + '/patterns/record-detail'}>record
    detail</a>, <a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>object page</a>, and
    <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a> — and they were built
    independently, for different reasons, in different slices. Compared
    afterward, they had already converged on the same four regions. That
    convergence is the contract on this page: not a new pattern, and not a new
    component — the decision a screen author no longer has to make twice.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The four regions</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
    <table class="bo-data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Region</th>
          <th scope="col">What it answers</th>
          <th scope="col">Built from</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Identity</strong></td>
          <td>What is this, and what state is it in right now?</td>
          <td><a href={base + '/components/badge'}>Badge</a> for status, a title</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Facts</strong></td>
          <td>The small fixed set the reader needs before doing anything else.</td>
          <td><a href={base + '/components/kv'}>Kv</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>History</strong></td>
          <td>How did it get here — what happened, in order?</td>
          <td><a href={base + '/components/approval-workflow'}>Timeline or audit trail</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Action</strong></td>
          <td>What can the reader do about it, and where does that live on screen?</td>
          <td><a href={base + '/components/form'}>Form actions</a>, wizard controls, or nothing (read-only)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">All four are shipped primitives. This page names
    an order and a set of slots — it adds no CSS and no component.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Which of the three patterns — decided by two questions, not by taste</h2>
    <p>The content that actually removes a decision from a screen author isn't
    the four regions above — every ERP detail screen already has some version
    of them. It's knowing <strong>which pattern to reach for</strong>, before
    writing any markup:</p>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Is the current moment itself a decision someone must make</strong>
      — approve, reject, sign off? Use
      <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a>. Its anatomy is the
      same four regions, but History and Action share the screen with a queue,
      because the reader is choosing, not just reading.</li>
      <li><strong>Otherwise: how long is the record?</strong> Short enough to
      take in on one scroll (a handful of facts, a short history) →
      <a href={base + '/patterns/record-detail'}>record detail</a>. Long enough
      that the reader needs to jump between sections rather than scroll through
      all of them → <a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>object page</a>,
      which adds in-page navigation and a collapsing header — built because a
      short-record layout stops working past a certain length (roadmap 52.2).</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Answering those two questions is the whole
    choice. Nothing below this page is a third option — a screen that doesn't
    fit either fork is a new pattern, not a variant of these three, and earns
    its own Accept criteria the way every pattern here does.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Where each pattern spends the four regions differently</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
    <table class="bo-data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Region</th>
          <th scope="col"><a href={base + '/patterns/record-detail'}>Record detail</a></th>
          <th scope="col"><a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>Object page</a></th>
          <th scope="col"><a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>Approval</a></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Identity</td>
          <td>Breadcrumb + title</td>
          <td>Sticky header, title + badge</td>
          <td>Stepper's current step</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Facts</td>
          <td>Facts strip (<code>.bo-kv</code>)</td>
          <td>Collapsing kv strip under the header</td>
          <td>Record summary — just enough to decide without leaving</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>History</td>
          <td>Record feed, then status timeline + audit trail</td>
          <td>One section among several, reached via the anchor bar</td>
          <td>Status timeline is the primary content, not a supporting one; audit trail is append-only underneath it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Action</td>
          <td>Feed input (add a record: receipt, invoice, or note)</td>
          <td>Sticky footer action bar</td>
          <td>Decision cluster (Approve / Reject) opening a dialog, plus the queue for what's next</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/patterns/record-detail", "Record detail"],
    ["/patterns/object-page", "Object page"],
    ["/patterns/approval", "Approval"],
    ["/patterns/value-help", "Value help"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
